  "id": "Compound::DB00232 - Gene::6559",
  "verbalization": "Methyclothiazide, a thiazide diuretic, is consistently linked to Slc12a3 through a shared lineage in the hetionet dataset. The evidence suggests that Methyclothiazide, as part of the thiazide class, binds to Slc12a3 through a common ancestor in the thiazide diuretic family. This relationship is reinforced by multiple paths that trace Methyclothiazide through different thiazide derivatives, such as Polythiazide and Bendroflumethiazide, all of which exhibit a binding interaction with Slc12a3. The lowest common ancestors across these paths point to thiazide diuretics and benzothiadiazine compounds, indicating a broader functional relationship between thiazide drugs and Slc12a3. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which thiazide diuretics influence Slc12a3, possibly through shared pharmacological targets or regulatory pathways.",
